{"id":"mahabharata-13-030","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":30,"title":"त्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 30 · Matanga is refused again","summary":{"en":"Grieved, Matanga goes to Gaya and stands on his toe for a hundred years, and Indra tells him again that brahmanhood is out of reach. He gives Matanga another boon, a name that will be honoured by women and a place of fame, and says that this is the word of the great Indra.","kn":"ದುಃಖಿತ ಮತಂಗ ಗಯೆಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ ಹೆಬ್ಬೆರಳಿನಲ್ಲಿ ನೂರು ವರ್ಷ ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಇಂದ್ರ ಮತ್ತೆ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣತ್ವ ಅಸಾಧ್ಯವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ವರವಾಗಿ ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರಿಂದ ಗೌರವಿಸಲ್ಪಡುವ ಹೆಸರು, ಕೀರ್ತಿಯ ಸ್ಥಾನ ನೀಡಿ ಇದು ಮಹೇಂದ್ರನ ಮಾತೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"दुखी मतंग गया जाकर अँगूठे पर सौ वर्ष खड़े रहते हैं, और इन्द्र फिर कहते हैं कि ब्राह्मणत्व पहुँच से बाहर है। वे मतंग को दूसरा वर देते हैं कि उसका नाम स्त्रियों द्वारा आदृत होगा और कीर्ति का स्थान मिलेगा, और इसे महेन्द्र का वचन कहते हैं।","te":"దుఃఖితుడైన మతంగుడు గయ చేరి బొటనవేలిపై వంద ఏళ్లు నిలుస్తాడు, ఇంద్రుడు మళ్లీ బ్రాహ్మణత్వం అందదని చెబుతాడు. మరో వరంగా స్త్రీలచే గౌరవింపబడే పేరు, కీర్తి స్థానం ఇచ్చి ఇది మహేంద్రుని మాటని అంటాడు.","ta":"வருந்திய மதங்கன் கயை சென்று பெருவிரலில் நூறாண்டுகள் நிற்க, இந்திரன் மீண்டும் அந்தணத்துவம் எட்டாதது என்று கூறுகிறான். வேறு வரமாகப் பெண்களால் போற்றப்படும் பெயரையும் புகழுக்குரிய இடத்தையும் தந்து, இது மகேந்திரனின் சொல் என்கிறான்.","ml":"ദുഃഖിതനായ മാതംഗൻ ഗയയിലേക്ക് പോയി നൂറു വർഷം കാൽവിരലിൽ നിൽക്കുന്നു; ബ്രാഹ്മണ്യം വീണ്ടും അപ്രാപ്യമാണെന്ന് ഇന്ദ്രൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തോട് പറയുന്നു. സ്ത്രീകളാൽ ആദരിക്കപ്പെടുന്ന ഒരു നാമവും, പ്രശസ്തിയുള്ള ഒരു സ്ഥാനവുമായ മറ്റൊരു വരം ഇന്ദ്രൻ മാതംഗന് നൽകുന്നു; ഇത് മഹാനായ ഇന്ദ്രന്റെ വാക്കാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.30; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तो मतङ्गस्तु भृशं शोकपरायणः ।\nअतिष्ठत गयां गत्वा सोऽङ्गुष्ठेन शतं समाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, Matanga was sunk in grief. He went to Gaya and stood there on his big toe for a hundred years."}},{"n":2,"text":"सुदुष्करं वहन्योगं कृशो धमनिसंततः ।\nत्वगस्थिभूतो धर्मात्मा स पपातेति नः श्रुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Practicing that very hard discipline, he grew thin, his veins stood out, and he was only skin and bones. We have heard that the righteous man then collapsed."}},{"n":3,"text":"तं पतन्तमभिद्रुत्य परिजग्राह वासवः ।\nवराणामीश्वरो दाता सर्वभूतहिते रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he fell, Indra rushed up and caught him, Indra the lord and giver of boons, who delights in the good of all beings."}},{"text":"शक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"मतङ्ग ब्राह्मणत्वं ते संवृतं परिपन्थिभिः ।\nपूजयन्सुखमाप्नोति दुःखमाप्नोत्यपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Matanga, the status of a brahmin is barred to you by those who stand in its way. One who honors brahmins finds happiness; one who dishonors them finds sorrow."}},{"n":5,"text":"ब्राह्मणे सर्वभूतानां योगक्षेमः समाहितः ।\nब्राह्मणेभ्योऽनुतृप्यन्ति पितरो देवतास्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The welfare and security of all beings rest with the brahmin. The ancestors and the gods are satisfied through brahmins."}},{"n":6,"text":"ब्राह्मणः सर्वभूतानां मतङ्ग पर उच्यते ।\nब्राह्मणः कुरुते तद्धि यथा यद्यच्च वाञ्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Matanga, the brahmin is called the highest among all beings, for a brahmin brings about whatever he wishes, just as he wishes."}},{"n":7,"text":"बह्वीस्तु संसरन्योनीर्जायमानः पुनः पुनः ।\nपर्याये तात कस्मिंश्चिद्ब्राह्मण्यमिह विन्दति ॥","meaning":{"en":"My son, born again and again through many wombs, a being gains brahminhood here only at some turn of that cycle."}},{"text":"मतङ्ग उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Matanga said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"किं मां तुदसि दुःखार्तं मृतं मारयसे च माम् ।\nतं तु शोचामि यो लब्ध्वा ब्राह्मण्यं न बुभूषते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Why do you torment me, who am afflicted with sorrow? You are killing one already dead. I grieve rather for the man who gains brahminhood and does not wish to live up to it."}},{"n":9,"text":"ब्राह्मण्यं यदि दुष्प्रापं त्रिभिर्वर्णैः शतक्रतो ।\nसुदुर्लभं तदावाप्य नानुतिष्ठन्ति मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra, if brahminhood is so hard for the three other classes to reach, then people who win that rare thing and do not practice it are most to be pitied."}},{"n":10,"text":"यः पापेभ्यः पापतमस्तेषामधम एव सः ।\nब्राह्मण्यं योऽवजानीते धनं लब्ध्वेव दुर्लभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever scorns brahminhood, as one scorns hard-won wealth, is the worst even among the worst of sinners."}},{"n":11,"text":"दुष्प्रापं खलु विप्रत्वं प्राप्तं दुरनुपालनम् ।\nदुरवापमवाप्यैतन्नानुतिष्ठन्ति मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Priesthood is truly hard to win, and once won, hard to keep. Having obtained it, people still do not act upon it."}},{"n":12,"text":"एकारामो ह्यहं शक्र निर्द्वंद्वो निष्परिग्रहः ।\nअहिंसादमदानस्थः कथं नार्हामि विप्रताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra, I live alone in a grove, free of the pairs of opposites, owning nothing, and firm in non-violence and self-control. Why do I not deserve brahminhood?"}},{"n":13,"text":"यथाकामविहारी स्यां कामरूपी विहंगमः ।\nब्रह्मक्षत्राविरोधेन पूजां च प्राप्नुयामहम् ।\nयथा ममाक्षया कीर्तिर्भवेच्चापि पुरंदर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let me roam wherever I please, take any form I wish, and move through the sky like a bird. Let me gain honor without clashing with brahmins or kshatriyas, and let my fame be undying, Indra."}},{"text":"इन्द्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Indra said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"छन्दोदेव इति ख्यातः स्त्रीणां पूज्यो भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will be known as Chandodeva, and women will honor you."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"एवं तस्मै वरं दत्त्वा वासवोऽन्तरधीयत ।\nप्राणांस्त्यक्त्वा मतङ्गोऽपि प्राप तत्स्थानमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having granted him this boon, Indra vanished. Matanga too gave up his life and reached that highest state."}},{"n":16,"text":"एवमेतत्परं स्थानं ब्राह्मण्यं नाम भारत ।\nतच्च दुष्प्रापमिह वै महेन्द्रवचनं यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, Bharata, brahminhood is a supreme state, and it is hard to attain in this world, as Indra's words showed."}}]}]}